@page "/triage-demo"
@layout ShowroomLayout

@* The triage demo (F106.3.4; in the showroom since F127.1): one real error of the made-up order service, triaged by
   the team and recorded once, played back step by step with the agent at work lit and a popup per step, then the
   offer. The player shows its own steps, so the stage gives it the whole width and no cues. A live run takes its
   place when the workflow lands (F106.3.3). *@

<PageTitle>Watch a triage · louis-agent</PageTitle>
<PageHead Description="Watch a team of louis-agent agents triage a real error: sort it, find the cause, fix it on a branch with a test and review the fix." />

<DemoStage Accent="TileAccent.Purple" Kicker="Agents at work · The triage team">
    <Title>Watch a team triage a real error.</Title>
    <Lede>
        A made-up order service failed on a retired discount code. A team of agents sorts the error, decides what it
        gets, finds the cause, fixes it on a branch with a test, and reviews the fix, while code between them checks
        every step. <span class="stage-made-up">This is that run, recorded once and played back. Nothing runs while
            you watch.</span>
    </Lede>
    <Player>
        <TriagePlayer Source="recordings/triage-run.jsonl">
            <Actions>
                <GuideButton Class="is-plain" Question="I watched the triage team fix the order service. What just happened, and could I get a team like that?">Ask the guide what happened</GuideButton>
            </Actions>
        </TriagePlayer>
    </Player>
    <Offer>
        <span>Want a team like this on your own services?</span>
        <a href="/contact">Ask for yours →</a>
    </Offer>
</DemoStage>
